  "grammar": {
    "title": "8B: Reporting what people say",
    "explanation": "When someone speaks, we can tell others about it. We use **said** to report what people said.\n\nWe change I to he or she. We change love to **loved** and is to **was**.\n\nSo 'I love cake' becomes 'she loved cake', and 'the cookie is sweet' becomes 'the cookie was sweet'.",
    "examples": [
      "Anna says, *I love cake.* Then we tell a friend: Anna said she loved cake.",
      "Mom says, *The cookie is sweet.* Then we say: Mom said the cookie was sweet. (the cookie = today's word)",
      "Dan says, *Pizza is my dinner.* Then we say: Dan said pizza was his dinner.",
      "Lena says, *I drink juice.* Then we say: Lena said she drank juice. (drink changes to drank)",
      "Sam says, *Breakfast is important.* Then we say: Sam said breakfast was important."
    ],
    "practice": [
      {
        "q": "Anna says, 'I love pizza.' What do you tell your friend?",
        "a": "Anna said she loved pizza."
      },
      {
        "q": "Mom says, 'The cake is sweet.' What do you tell your friend?",
        "a": "Mom said the cake was sweet."
      },
      {
